# R47 (docs/R47-repo-hygiene.md): core.autocrlf=true plus no .gitattributes meant
# every tracked text file checked out as CRLF on Windows, which is a Prettier
# violation (LF-configured) on every single line — the buried signal that hid
# four real lint errors. `eol=lf` normalizes storage and checkout to LF for text
# files regardless of the checking-out machine's own autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never text-normalize these — corrupts binary image formats.
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.png binary

# R179 — fixtures whose whole point is their line endings. `eol=lf` above would
# rewrite these to LF on commit and on every checkout, leaving a file that reads
# as a CRLF fixture, is named as one, and is not one: the tests built on it would
# pass while asserting nothing. `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both
# directions so the bytes committed are the bytes checked out, on every platform.
# `test/crlfFixture.test.ts` asserts that this rule is actually in force, because
# a silently-normalized fixture is indistinguishable from a working one.
test/fixtures/crlf/** -text
